  "notes": [
    "All clips are normalized poses over frame_range; scrub by normalized time for state, play for recoil.",
    "Clips are sparse/composable: each touches only its listed targets; apply several at once.",
    "Rudder is SYMMETRIC: 0=hard port, 0.5=center (frame 15), 1=hard starboard.",
    "Guns: 0=STOWED (pulled in 0.15m, barrels clear the closed lids), 1=READY (run out at port). Recoil reuses this same travel (kick from ready toward stowed ~0.15m).",
    "ORDERING: to CLOSE a port, set gun stowed (Gun=0) THEN close lid (Lid=0). To OPEN for action, open lid (Lid=1) THEN run gun out (Gun=1).",
    "Lids: 0=CLOSED (flush to hull; each lid has its own baked toe-in to follow the hull curve), 1=OPEN. Closed is the default; init lid clips at frame 0 on load.",
    "Sail furl + its paired sheet morph must be driven to the same value (see sail_sheet_pairs).",
    "Morph weights can be driven directly (0..1) instead of via Furl_* clips.",
    "B_Flag, B_Pennant, B_Wheel have no clip - rotate in code.",
    "MAST DAMAGE (see mast_damage): scrub 'MastDown' 0->1 by mast-zone damage (0=intact, 0.5=cracked/leaning, 1=collapsed over the PORT rail, snapping low at the deck). Ramp the 'Break' morph on Sloop_Mast near full for the splintered snap. The whole rig topples as a unit (yard/boom/gaff/flag/pennant bones are children of the new B_Mast hinge); standing rigging + the two headsails are skinned to B_Mast with a foot->hull gradient so they drag down with the mast but their feet stay attached to the hull. Costs +1 draw (Sloop_Mast = one Atlas_C primitive); no new materials."
  ],
